[statement]
The preliminary choices take the request's names before the world's:
`y`, requested, is chosen first, for `p2`, which provides the world's `x`
too, so `x` takes `p2` and the installed `p1` is removed. Decisions still
go in name order (`world-and-request-names-are-decided-in-name-order`).

[repository]
P:p1
V:1
p:x
k:100

P:p2
V:1
p:x y=1
k:10

P:p3
V:1
p:y=1

[installed]
P:p1
V:1
p:x
k:100

[world]
x

[request]
y

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
remove p1 1
install p2 1
